      "alerts": [
        {
          "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
          "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 20 at 2:52PM PST until November 26 at 4:00PM PST by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Minor",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "* WHAT...Up to 3.0 ft of inundation above ground level is\npossible in low-lying areas near shorelines and tidal waterways.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal North Bay Including Point Reyes National\nSeashore, San Francisco Peninsula Coast, Northern Monterey Bay\nand Southern Monterey Bay and Big Sur Coast Counties.\n\n* WHEN...From 4 AM Saturday to 4 PM PST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...High tides will result in flooding of low-lying\ninfrastructure, isolated road closures, and coastal erosion.\nRising tides will bring water and waves farther up the beach\nthan normal, restricting escape from beaches and coastal areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...At the San Francisco tidal gauge, high tide\nis expected to be 1.5 ft above normal (7.3 ft MLLW) at 8:15 AM\nSaturday, 2.1 ft above normal (7.9 ft MLLW) at 8:48 AM Sunday,\n2.3 ft above normal (8.1 ft MLLW) at 9:25 AM Monday, 2.9 ft\nabove normal (8.7 ft MLLW) at 10:05 AM Tuesday, 3.0 ft above\nnormal (8.8 ft MLLW) at 10:49 AM Wednesday, and 2.6 ft above\nnormal (8.4 ft MLLW) at 11:38 AM Thursday. These predictions\ninclude up to 1.8 ft of surge that will enhance the astronomical\ntide and flooding threat. High tide varies up to 90 minutes\nearlier or later along the Pacific Coast and through the San\nFrancisco Bay, respectively.",
